<title>USA: U.S. FY97 budget deficit seen below $144 billion.</title>
<headline>U.S. FY97 budget deficit seen below $144 billion.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Office of Management and Budget Director Franklin Raines said on Monday that he expected the fiscal year 1997 U.S. budget deficit to be lower than the $144 billion estimated in March.</p>
<p>&quot;We estimated in March $144 billion. It would certainly be lower than that,&quot; Raines told reporters in St. Louis, where President Bill Clinton is campaigning.</p>
</text>
